Brother's original Linux driver

Brother Industries' own Linux driver package (LPR filter, CUPS wrapper
sources, and i386 ELF binaries) was kept locally as a protocol reference
during development. It is Brother's own material, is not included in this
repository, and is not linked into SisterHL2030.

  - cupswrapper / filter / psconvert2 / brcupsconfig sources: GNU GPL v2
    or later, Copyright (C) 2003–2006 Brother Industries, Ltd.
  - rawtobr2, libbrcomplpr2.so, brprintconflsr2, braddprinter: proprietary
    ELF i386 binaries. Used only as a reverse-engineering reference under
    authorization from Brother. They are not redistributed as part of the
    compiled driver.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Protocol documentation

The HL-2030 job format (PJL envelope, PCL language, compression mode
1030, band layout) was recovered from libbrcomplpr2.so and rawtobr2.
Peter De Wachter's brlaser (GPL-2+) independently documented the same
mode-1030 line codec; that published description was used as a
cross-check. See docs/protocol.md and docs/reverse-engineering.md.
